The design surface's right-click menu had grown to 33 items. Like WPF's, it
now keeps at the top what acts on the selection (edit, code, select, hide /
lock, align / order, group, reset to DFM, the mode) and folds the rest:
- 顯示: names, wiring marks, DFM place, Tab order, grid, zoom to fit, 100%
- 檢查與比對: wiring overview, DFM difference list, check this page, fix
  every cut attribute
25 top-level items now. The command palette and title bar are unchanged.

README / CHEATSHEET say where each item is now ("右鍵「顯示 → …」"); the
README's right-click row lists the whole menu.

Test: smoke (the moved items are only in their submenus, <= 25 top-level
items, and every command any menu names is declared and registered).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
